Spec: Holiday entity

Purpose:
  The Holiday entity: a date and a title. A view-less, route-less package used by ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  ../semester/semester.sdd and ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd

Must:
  A Holiday has a date and a title. Its date is indexed for range listings.
  A Holiday has no foreign key: holidays are global to the calendar, not owned by a Semester or a Course.
  @HolidayService.add_holiday rejects an empty title with @InvalidHolidayError before storage.
  @HolidayRepository in ./ports.py exposes operations to list holidays for a date range and to add one.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist.

Tasks:
  [?] Decide whether a Holiday can be deleted or edited after creation
  [x] Implement @Holiday in ./domain.py and a hardcoded ./services.py returning one placeholder Holiday within the
    hardcoded Semester's date range, standing in for @HolidayRepository until persistence exists
  [x] Replace the hardcoded ./services.py with a class-based @HolidayRepository-backed `HolidayService`
    (./ports.py and ./repository_sqlite.py), per ../architecture.sdd's Example
  [x] Reject empty Holiday titles in @HolidayService.add_holiday with @InvalidHolidayError
